==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|миръ||ru-PRO}} (only in the sense of “peace”)
* {{alter|ru|міръ||ru-PRO}} (only in the sense of “universe, world”)

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*mirъ||peace; world}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*meiˀrás|t=peace}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro||*mey(H)-ró-s}}.

Russian uses the regular dual meaning of "peace" and "world" that was usual in Old Slavic; this Slavic feature considered unique. The peace/world ambiguity is saved in some other Slavic languages, such as Bulgarian, but with the sense of "world" it remains there as a dated or poetic term.

The pre-1918 orthography had an orthographical distinction of the two identically pronounced words to avoid confusion (see Alternative forms).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-мир.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-мир.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|c|loc=+|adj=мирово́й,мирско́й|dim=миро́к}}
[[File:Krasnogorsk-2013 - panoramio (1040).jpg|thumb|'''Миру''' — '''мир'''!]]

# {{lb|ru|usually|uncountable}} [[peace]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[война́]] [[и]] '''мир'''|war and '''peace'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[опло́т]] '''ми́ра'''|stronghold '''of peace'''}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''мир''' [[во]] [[всём]] ми́ре|world '''peace'''|lit= '''peace''' throughout all the world|q=the first "мир" is "peace", the second "мир" in the prepositional case is "world"}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[w:ru:Миру — мир!|Ми́ру — '''мир'''!]]|'''Peace''' to the world! ({{n-g|Soviet slogan}})|q=the first "мир" in the dative case is "world", the second "мир" is "peace"}}
#: {{ux|ru|Же́нщины ми́ра! Крепи́те еди́нство в борьбе́ за '''мир'''.|q= the first "мир" in the genitive case is "world", the second "мир" in the accusative case is "peace"|Women of the world! Strengthen unity in the struggle for '''peace'''. ({{n-g|from a 1978 [https://catalog.shm.ru/entity/OBJECT/2957428 poster] by Mikhail Getman}})}}
# [[universe]]; [[world]]; [[planet]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[происхожде́ние]] '''ми́ра'''|origin '''of the universe'''}}
#: {{ux|ru|мир [[во]] [[всём]] '''ми́ре'''|'''world''' peace|lit= peace throughout all '''the world'''|q=slogan, the first "мир" is "peace", the second "мир" in the prepositional case is "world"}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Ми́ру''' — мир!|Peace '''to the world'''!  ({{n-g|slogan}})|q=the first "мир" in the dative case is "world", the second "мир" is "peace"}}
#: {{ux|ru|Же́нщины '''ми́ра'''! Крепи́те еди́нство в борьбе́ за мир.|q= the first "мир" in the genitive case is "world", the second "мир" in the accusative case is "peace"|Women '''of the world'''! Strengthen unity in the struggle for peace. ({{n-g|from a 1978 [https://catalog.shm.ru/entity/OBJECT/2957428 poster] by Mikhail Getman}})}}

====Usage notes====
The locative form {{m|ru|миру́}}, "(in [this]) world", is used with religious figures to indicate their secular name – for example, "Протопоп Афанасий, в миру Александр Иванович Неизвестнов" would mean "Protopope Afanasy, secular name Alexander Ivanovich Neizvestnov".

